# Copy the current machine under a new name through the printer settings window and
# assert that the window says it saved. What the copy is worth is asserted outside
# the window: tools/check deletes the preset this writes, counts the values it
# carries and resolves its profiles headlessly.
#
#   cockpit start next-layer --model oracle/models/cube_20.stl \
#       --arg=--preset-dialog --arg=printer
#   cockpit run tools/cockpit/scripts/next-layer-save-as.drive
#
# Nothing is edited before Save as, on purpose: "nothing has been changed, so there
# is nothing to save" is the report this proves gone, and it came from a copy that
# wrote only the diff. The name field is at a fixed place in the 1920x1080 window,
# (1250,190), read off a capture; Ctrl+A clears whatever the field already held.
assert-text "Printer settings"
shot /tmp/cockpit-saveas-0-window.png
click 1250 190
key A --modifier ctrl
type "Gate Save As"
click-text "Save as"
find-text "saved Gate Save As"
shot /tmp/cockpit-saveas-1-saved.png
